GEARED ELBOW: J3 servo moved 27.20 mm toward the wrist (y -17.80) and 10.80 mm out
   gear turns at r 19.40, pinion at r 10.40, both in the 10.80 band off the plate face
   the pinion circle (r 10.40) is taller than the lobe (8.70), so the standoff
   survives only as a web at the WRIST end, y -7.40 .. 5.45 - 12.85 mm of it
   608ZZ: 21.98 pocket x 7.0 deep from the plate INNER face, 0.50 shoulder
   shoulder bores 13.0 - OUTSIDE the 12.0 inner race, so the stationary plate bears on the OUTER one
   J3 drive-side flange counterbore DELETED - j3_gear has no flange and its journal is built for the full 7.5 plate
   the servo PAD is not here - it is j3_servo_cap, 6.7 thick, bolted to this web
   by 2 x M3 at y 5.02, z +/-4.10, 2.6 pilot x 8.0 deep. Without that split
   the gear, the pinion and the retention M3 could none of them be fitted - GATE j3_installs.

J4 DRIVE: no horn. wrist_hub bores onto the SG90 spline and seats 0.40 off the case top,
   so the lobe is 7.10 thick (servo stack 6.70 + running gap 0.40) against 6.70 before. The case top now sits 0.40 OUTBOARD of the plate outer face and the hub seats ON it - the wrist does not move, the arm is 0.40 wider
   THE FLANGE NEVER FITTED THE ONE-STEP WINDOW: tab plate 32.30 long against a 23.70 window, overhanging 4.30 at EACH end onto solid lobe - GATE servo_fit MEASURED 195.75 mm3 of MG90S in that band. Re-run 2026-09-03 against the SG90 that replaced it, this lobe reads 0.0 - the double cut below is what fixed it, and it fixed it for the smaller case too
   SO THE LOBE IS CUT TWICE: case window 23.70 x 13.20 deep 4.70, then a flange recess 32.80 x 13.20 deep 2.40 to the tab plane at 27.00
   walls left: end 1.60, side 2.10, fillet corner 1.60, all against MIN_WALL 1.60 - fa_lobe_pad 4.10 and fa_lobe_radius_j4 2.10 are DERIVED from those three floors, not chosen
   pilots 1.8 x 3.00 deep FROM THE RECESS FLOOR, leaving 1.70 to fa_plate_out and the J4 flange counterbore behind it
   J3 STACK UNCHANGED: fa_cap_t 6.70 and fa_j3_standoff 10.80 both still read fa_lobe_t, so the cap thickness and the pinion plane did not move
   BUT J3 IS NOT DONE. No recess is cut in the J3 lobe here and none is wanted: that lobe carries no servo any more, only the standoff web. The J3 SERVO sits on j3_servo_cap, which cuts its window through the full fa_cap_t at a tighter clearance still, so it has this same flange landing on solid pad - and it is not this file. What it gets from here is the pad: it reads fa_lobe_pad, now 4.10, which is exactly the room a 32.80 recess needs.

WEB ON THE CENTRELINE: 6.2 mm between the two swings (J4 takes 25.4, J3 takes 13.4)
